# Review routing for this repository (TD-019's hygiene list).
#
# GitHub needs a **user or a team** here; an organisation name alone is not a valid owner. This
# organisation has no teams — `gh api orgs/gtfo-ai/teams` answered `[]` on 2026-09-15 — and three
# members, so the owner below is the maintainer who has written the tree. When a team exists, the
# whole file becomes one line naming it.
#
# Every pattern matches at any depth unless it starts with `/`, and the **last** matching pattern
# wins — the opposite of `.gitignore`'s first-match rule and of the anchoring convention this
# repository follows for ignore files. The order below is therefore general first, specific last.
#
# This is *not* the reviewer routing the pipeline reads. That one is the **target project's**
# `CODEOWNERS`, parsed by `packages/integrations/src/git/codeowners.ts` for WP-37's risk classes.

* @JanMikes

# The three things that decide what the product is, and what it may do. A change here is a
# decision, not an edit: `docs/decisions/**` is the record, `docs/technical/**` the spec the code
# is held to, and the workflows are what gates every push.
/docs/decisions/ @JanMikes
/docs/technical/ @JanMikes
/.github/ @JanMikes

# Release engineering: the version, the changelog, the release workflow and the third-party
# accounting a published image carries (TD-019, BD-002).
/release-please-config.json @JanMikes
/.release-please-manifest.json @JanMikes
/CHANGELOG.md @JanMikes
/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md @JanMikes
/LICENSE @JanMikes
/NOTICE @JanMikes

# The schema is forward-only and an applied file is never edited (TD-011).
/packages/infrastructure/src/db/migrations/ @JanMikes
